Implemented `transpose(text)` in `transpose.py`.

**Approach** (researched canonical Exercism transpose problem + reference solution): pad each line to the longest width on the right with a sentinel char (guaranteed absent from the input), transpose the resulting rectangle column-by-column, then strip trailing sentinels and convert the rest back to spaces. This makes padding distinct from real characters, which is what the prompt's rules require: pad to the left (`AB\nDEF` → `AD\nBE\n F`), don't pad to the right (`ABC\nDE` → `AD\nBE\nC`), and preserve every input character (real spaces kept, `_` untouched). It also handles the empty string (the reference solution crashes on it).

